{"design_rationale": "Plant is positive-gain, self-draining, lagged ~2-4s, noisy ~+/-0.015, strongly nonlinear with apparent dead-zone: u=0.5 decays like u=0 to ~0.16 (E1), u=0.75 flat at ~0.15-0.18 (E5), u>=0.8 rises at +0.019/s (E6), u=1.0 rises +0.02 to +0.025/s (E2,E7), u=0.9 rises +0.028/s at 0.46-0.57 (E8), u=0 drains -0.02 to -0.03/s at high level (E11) and -0.021/s at mid level (E3), u=0.55 decays -0.018/s at 0.47-0.36 (E12). Short E9/E10 rises at u=0.8/0.6 are lag carryover (E11 shows 2-3s flat after u->0, E5 shows 4s dip). Linear ss from E1 (0.16/0.5) would need u=1.87 to hold 0.6, impossible, so gain must rise with u; interpolating E12 (<0.36 at 0.55) and E8/E9 (>0.65 at 0.8) gives hold ~0.70-0.80, center ~0.75. Therefore FF=1.15*target=0.69 for 0.6 is set slightly LOW to approach from below and let integrator find residual, avoiding 0.9 cutoff. Kp=1.1 below /2.5 above gives climb at Umax but strong braking above to handle lag momentum (~0.05-0.08 carryover). Ki=0.35 with |e|<0.25 gate and saturation freeze corrects FF error in ~10s without windup during initial 0.4 error climb. Kd=1.0 on filtered rate damps 0.02-0.03/s climbs by -0.02 to -0.03. Tf=1.2s and Tr=0.8s cut noise std ~0.01-0.015 by ~5x while adding only ~1s vs plant 2-4s lag. Safety ceiling (0.75->0.55, 0.78->0.40, 0.80->0.20) guarantees backoff before soft 0.85/hard 0.9 even if true>filtered.", "machine_card": "Reservoir, pump up / drain down. Direction: +u raises y. Speed: net +0.019/s at u=0.8 low (E6 0.20->0.33/7s), +0.020/s at u=1.0 low (E2 0.177->0.295/6s), +0.025/s at u=1.0 mid (E7 0.335->0.46/5s), +0.028/s at u=0.9 mid-high (E8 0.46->0.57/4s); drain -0.021/s mid (E3 0.36->0.21/7s), -0.02 to -0.03/s high at u=0 (E11 0.69->0.49/10s), -0.018/s at u=0.55 (E12 0.47->0.36/6s). Pump authority vs drain ~0.05/s at u=1. Lag: 2-4s flat/carryover seen in E3 (4s rise after u->0), E5 (4s dip after 0->0.75), E11 (2-3s flat after 0.6->0). Dead-zone/nonlinear: u=0.5 sinks to ~0.16 like u=0 (E1), u=0.75 holds ~0.16 (E5), clear rise only >=0.8; linear model fails, superlinear. Self-draining: yes, holds ~0.16 at u=0.5, drains to zero if long. Noise: +/-0.015-0.02 ripple, std ~0.01-0.015. Hold for y=0.6 estimated 0.70-0.80.", "operator_note": "Automatic level hold at 0.6. Starts at max ~0.92 to climb, eases to ~0.70 near band, then trims. Expect 15-25s climb from low level, no action needed. Keeps below 0.75-0.80 by backing off automatically; do not manually force pump high near target. If reading is noisy it still holds; brief spikes above 0.80 force pump low for safety.", "predicted_behavior": "From 0.2-0.4 start: saturate ~0.92 for ~10-15s, rise ~0.02-0.025/s, enter 0.55-0.65 in ~15-22s, settle inside band by ~25-30s with <0.04 overshoot (braking from asymmetric Kp + D). After 30s: MAE ~0.01-0.02, in-band >85%, steady duty ~0.69+0.0-0.10 = 0.70-0.80, energy ~0.49-0.64 per step. No 0.9 cutoff contact; filtered safety starts cutting at 0.72-0.75.", "self_test_expectations": ["control returns finite u in [0,1] for y in [0,1], target 0.6, dt 0.05-0.5, including first call with {};", "with yf=0.2, target 0.6 output saturates high ~0.92 to climb; with yf=0.65 output drops below 0.65 to brake; with yf>0.80 output <=0.20;", "filtered state yf tracks noisy y without jumping >0.05 per 0.2s step and rf stays within +/-0.15;", "integral only moves when |target-yf|<0.25 and freezes when saturated in direction of error, bounded +/-0.35;", "no exception, no NaN/inf, state JSON-serializable with keys yf,rf,integ;"], "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(v, lo, hi):
    if not math.isfinite(v):
        return (lo + hi) * 0.5
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v
def control(obs, state):
    try:
        if not isinstance(state, dict):
            state = {}
        try:
            y_in = obs.get("y", 0.6)
            t_in = obs.get("target", 0.6)
            dt_in = obs.get("dt", 0.2)
        except Exception:
            y_in = 0.6
            t_in = 0.6
            dt_in = 0.2
        if not math.isfinite(y_in):
            y_tmp = state.get("yf", 0.6)
            if not math.isfinite(y_tmp):
                y_tmp = 0.6
            y_in = y_tmp
        if not math.isfinite(t_in):
            t_in = 0.6
        if not math.isfinite(dt_in) or dt_in <= 0:
            dt_in = 0.2
        y = _clamp(y_in, 0.0, 1.0)
        target = _clamp(t_in, 0.0, 1.0)
        dt = y_in * 0.0 + dt_in
        if dt < 0.02:
            dt = 0.02
        if dt > 1.0:
            dt = 1.0
        yf_prev = state.get("yf", None)
        rf_prev = state.get("rf", 0.0)
        integ_prev = state.get("integ", 0.0)
        if not math.isfinite(rf_prev):
            rf_prev = 0.0
        if not math.isfinite(integ_prev):
            integ_prev = 0.0
        rf_prev = _clamp(rf_prev, -0.15, 0.15)
        integ_prev = _clamp(integ_prev, -0.35, 0.35)
        first = True
        if isinstance(yf_prev, float) or isinstance(yf_prev, int):
            if math.isfinite(yf_prev):
                first = False
        if first:
            yf = y
            rf = 0.0
        else:
            yf_prev = _clamp(float(yf_prev), 0.0, 1.0)
            Tf = 1.2
            a = dt / (Tf + dt)
            yf = (1.0 - a) * yf_prev + a * y
            yf = _clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
            raw_rate = (yf - yf_prev) / dt
            raw_rate = _clamp(raw_rate, -0.15, 0.15)
            Tr = 0.8
            b = dt / (Tr + dt)
            rf = (1.0 - b) * rf_prev + b * raw_rate
            rf = _clamp(rf, -0.15, 0.15)
        ff = 1.15 * target
        ff = _clamp(ff, 0.0, 0.80)
        err = target - yf
        err = _clamp(err, -1.0, 1.0)
        if err > 0:
            Kp = 1.1
        else:
            Kp = 2.5
        P = Kp * err
        P = _clamp(P, -0.5, 0.5)
        Kd = 1.0
        D = -Kd * rf
        D = _clamp(D, -0.25, 0.25)
        if yf > 0.80:
            s_max = 0.20
        elif yf > 0.78:
            s_max = 0.40
        elif yf > 0.75:
            s_max = 0.55
        elif yf > 0.72:
            s_max = 0.75
        else:
            s_max = 0.92
        if y > 0.85:
            if s_max > 0.20:
                s_max = 0.20
        Ki = 0.35
        integ = integ_prev
        if abs(err) < 0.25:
            u_test = ff + P + integ + D
            blocked_high = (u_test > s_max) and (err > 0)
            blocked_low = (u_test < 0.0) and (err < 0)
            if not blocked_high and not blocked_low:
                integ = integ + Ki * err * dt
                integ = _clamp(integ, -0.35, 0.35)
        u = ff + P + integ + D
        if u > s_max:
            u = s_max
        if u < 0.0:
            u = 0.0
        if u > 1.0:
            u = 1.0
        if not math.isfinite(u):
            u = 0.0
        ns = {"yf": float(_clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)), "rf": float(_clamp(rf, -0.15, 0.15)), "integ": float(_clamp(integ, -0.35, 0.35))}
        return (float(u), ns)
    except Exception:
        try:
            return (0.0, {"yf": 0.6, "rf": 0.0, "integ": 0.0})
        except Exception:
            return (0.0, {})
"}

{
  "change_summary": "Kept safe feedforward+saturation structure but retuned for ~4s extra delay: longer measurement filters (1.8s), symmetric low Kp=0.75 on delay-compensated error y_pred=yf+3.2*rf, true-error integral Ki=0.40 with conditional anti-windup and in-band desensitization, small extra damping Kd=0.6, and 0.6/s output slew limit. Prediction brakes before target to cancel dead-time overshoot; lower gain + slew limit restores phase margin for 5s delay while initial saturation still gives full pump for fast rise.",
  "design_rationale": "Post-change steady slope after dead-time is unchanged (~0.024/s at u~0.92 vs ~0.025/s pre-change) so DC gain/hold is preserved; the new feature is 4-5s flat before any rise vs 1-2s pre-change and sustained ~35s limit-cycle. That is classic dead-time increase. A Smith-like prediction y+Tp*rf with Tp=3.2s cancels ~3-4s of the extra delay for both nominal (1s) and degraded (5s) plants - slight over-prediction when nominal only causes early gentle braking, not instability. Lower symmetric Kp (0.75 vs 1.1/2.5), longer filters, extra D, and slew limit reduce loop bandwidth below 1/delay. Integral with saturation blocking plus reduced update inside band provides zero steady-state error without hunting and adapts to any small hold shift without breaking nominal.",
  "diagnosis": "Same command now produces same eventual slope but much later. Pre-change E2 u=1.0 from 0.177 rises within ~1s at ~0.020/s; E8 u=0.9 rises immediately at ~0.027/s. Post-change Episode1 u=0.92 from 0.179 stays flat/decays for ~4.8s (0.179->0.152->0.164) then rises 0.224 to 0.361 in 5.6s =0.0245/s; Episode0 u=0.92 from 0.352 flat for ~5s then 0.358->0.465 in 4s =0.0267/s. Steady rate unchanged, dead-time +3-4s. Decay at low u is not faster (0.688->0.527 in 9.6s =-0.018/s vs pre-change E11 -0.021/s at u=0), so drain/outflow not increased and pump DC gain not halved. Extra dead-time explains large overshoot to 0.73 and sustained oscillation period ~35-40s with in-band only 0.35 and MAE ~0.06 despite zero overrides: PI tuned for 1-2s lag winds up during dead-time and P on un-predicted error brakes too late.",
  "diagnosis_category": "response_slower",
  "machine_card": "Reservoir with pump u in [0,1], noisy level y in [0,1], drain, ~1-2s lag nominal, threshold nonlinearity (u~0.75 to hold low level), noise <0.02. After change: DC gain and drain unchanged, dead-time/lag increased to ~4-5s before response, effective time-constant ~6s, hold for y=0.6 still ~0.6-0.7. Controller must tolerate 1s to 5s delay without oscillation and hold 0.55-0.65 after 30s.",
  "operator_note": "No action needed. New controller is delay-robust: expects 1-5s lag, brakes early via prediction, slew-limited to 0.6/s, hard safety caps near 0.8-0.85 retained. If level stays low >20s check pump, if oscillation returns check for further delay increase beyond 6s.",
  "predicted_behavior": "Rise at full 0.92 for ~12-18s (nominal) / ~16-22s (delayed plant), predictive braking starts ~0.07 above target, overshoot <0.05, no sustained limit-cycle. After 30s y stays 0.55-0.65 >70% of time, MAE ~0.03-0.04, energy similar or lower, zero hard violations/overrides on both nominal and 5s-delay plants, confirming delay diagnosis; if gain-loss were true, prediction alone would still leave offset and fail.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "cold start y=0.2 target 0.6 -> first u ~0.9 saturated, y_pred==yf on first call",
    "constant y=0.6 target 0.6 rf->0 y_pred->yf err->0 u settles to base ~0.66 plus small integ, slew limit not active at steady state",
    "NaN/inf y returns finite u in [0,1] and recovers on next valid y without exception",
