  "change_summary": "Retuned for +3s dead-time with delay-robust PI: longer filters (Tf/Tr 1.8->3.0s), prediction horizon 3.2->5.0s, Kp 0.75->0.50, Kd 0.6->0.45 with tight clamp, Ki 0.40->0.10 with +/-0.25 limits and freeze when |err|>0.25, base 1.10*target->1.20*target (~0.72) to reduce windup, rate limit 0.60/s->0.30/s. This keeps full 0.92 fill when far but brakes early and integrates slowly near target to stop delay-induced limit cycle.",
  "design_rationale": "Discovery shows same u=1.0 net rise ~0.02/s before and after, so gain/outflow unchanged. What changed is dead-time: E2 rise detectable in ~1.5-2s vs post-change traces flat for ~4.5-5s at u=0.92 before rise, and fall delayed similarly. Old Tp=3.2s under-predicts 5s delay, Kp+Ki too aggressive, integral winds to 0.4 during fill then over-corrects to 0.25, giving ~40s 0.50-0.73 oscillation (v1 in-band 0.35, v2 worse). New design keeps aggressive fill for time-to-band (<30s) but uses long-horizon prediction to cut early, small Ki with anti-windup to avoid windup during fill, heavy filtering + slow rate limit to stay stable for both 2s nominal and 5s delayed plant.",
